      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T20:42:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Matthias/Steve, Please have a look at this LKL patch (Linux Kernel Library - fuzzing tool). Should provide some additional test coverage for android-mainline.\n\nTheir approach looks good to me -- minimal impact on our kernel source. Tool is isolated to arch/lkl and tools/lkl directories with some new build.configs and a couple of fixes for their ARCH_LKL builds.\n\nReferences: go/lkl, https://g3doc.corp.google.com/company/teams/asa/areas/protect/redteam/lkl/g3doc/overview.md?cl\u003dhead",
      "revId": "49c0f6edbe90fea47001515465b42662ddfbf6e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
