      "writtenOn": "2022-06-27T20:38:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I included you in a discussion thread for the background behind of this work. In short: The LKL maintainers have done some effort upstreaming this to linux mainline, but got rejected. One specific reason they received is that this code is doing the similar thing as usermode linux. I\u0027ve chatted with @tavip (who is one of the LKL maintainer and CC\u0027ed in this CR). There are attempt to merge this one with usermode Linux but not very successful because there are some difference on the purposes.\n\nBy upstreaming this to ACK, we are hoping to demonstrate its uniqueness (kernel fuzzing and unit testing) and make it accepted by Linux mainline when it adopted wider by public.\n\nThe maintenance burden you mentioned does exist:\n\nWe are trying our best to localize the changes to dedicated source directory, so merge conflict from upsteam linux shouldn\u0027t be a big concern (until to the point where LKL github project upstreaming request gets accepted, but we can coordinate that for a one time merge).\n\nThe ABI change happen in mainline can be a concern as LKL is implemented as a linux architecture. We definitely need clarify the ownership/responsibilities so that when things are broken RedTeam/LKL maintainer should step up and take a effort of fixing things. I\u0027m working on some document clarifying this and will share it shortly.",
      "parentUuid": "f2418f68_8aa0e69a",
      "revId": "49c0f6edbe90fea47001515465b42662ddfbf6e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
